        "en": "Let $f(x) = x^2$ and $g(x) = x - 3$. Find $(f - g)(2)$.",
        "hi": "मान लीजिए $f(x) = x^2$ और $g(x) = x - 3$। $(f - g)(2)$ ज्ञात कीजिए।"
      },
      "answer": {
        "value": 5,
        "unit": null
      },
      "hints": [
        {
          "en": "Watch the sign of $g(2)$.",
          "hi": "$g(2)$ का चिह्न देखिए।"
        }
      ],
      "solution": {
        "feynman": {
          "en": "Find $f(2)$ and $g(2)$, then subtract.",
          "hi": "$f(2)$ और $g(2)$ निकालिए, फिर घटाइए।"
        },
        "steps": [
          {
            "en": "$f(2) = 4$ and $g(2) = -1$, so $(f - g)(2) = 4 - (-1) = 5$ (NCERT §2.4.2 (ii)).",
            "hi": "$f(2) = 4$ और $g(2) = -1$, अतः $(f - g)(2) = 4 - (-1) = 5$ (NCERT §2.4.2 (ii))।"
          }
        ],
        "shortcut": null,
        "shortcut_fails_when": null,
        "common_traps": [
          {
            "why": {
              "en": "$3$ comes from treating $g(2)$ as $+1$.",
              "hi": "$3$ तब आता है जब $g(2)$ को $+1$ मान लिया जाए।"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
